From: PinePhone firmware
Subject: [PATCH] opengles: EGL: wait for the previous page flip

Without vsync, a frame that is ready while the previous one still waits for
its page flip replaces the queued one: LVGL rendered up to 80 frames per
second on a 67 Hz panel, a quarter of them never shown. Wait for the flip
instead, so frames follow the display (the DRM EGL backend implements both).
---
--- a/src/drivers/opengles/lv_opengles_egl.c
+++ b/src/drivers/opengles/lv_opengles_egl.c
@@ -66,7 +66,9 @@
         return NULL;
     }
     ctx->interface = *interface;
-    ctx->vsync = false;
+    /*Wait for the previous page flip before queueing the next one: without it, frames
+     *that are still queued when the next one is ready are replaced and never shown*/
+    ctx->vsync = true;
 
     lv_result_t res = load_egl(ctx);
     if(res != LV_RESULT_OK) {
